[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]statistics_perf_view.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/statistics_perf_view.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-mj[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-mj/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Rust perf-log aggregation and binding[/bold #D7AFFF]                         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]core_perf_logs[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core_perf_logs: add a `perf_logs` module to the sibling Rust core that [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]reads the six durable TUI/launch perf JSONL logs with bounded tail [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]reads, aggregates them over a caller-supplied window into one composite [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]wire payload, and exposes it as the `perf_logs_query` Python binding.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Python perf facade and view model[/bold #D7AFFF]                             [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]stats_facade[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core_perf_logs[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]stats_facade: add the thin `sase.stats` adapter that calls the new Rust [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]binding, fans out the fixed telemetry-store query set, and builds one [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]immutable presentation-ready PerfView with status grading and coverage [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]notes.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Perf view registration and interaction[/bold #D7AFFF]                        [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]perf_view[dim] · [dim][/dim]after stats_facade[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]perf_view: register Perf as the eighth Statistics view — tab strip, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]numbered selection, description, legends, grouping modes, non-project [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]scope, lazy loading, and the contextual help methodology section.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Perf view rendering[/bold #D7AFFF]                                           [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]perf_render[dim] · [dim][/dim]after perf_view[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]perf_render: build the Perf renderable — the five hero tiles, the TUI [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]startup and stall panels, the grouped latency table, the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]data-and-instrumentation strip, and every degraded, partial, and empty [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]state.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Visual snapshots and documentation[/bold #D7AFFF]                            [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]perf_visuals[dim] · [dim][/dim]after perf_render[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]perf_visuals: add the PNG visual snapshots and their fixtures for the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]populated, narrow, and telemetry-disabled Perf states, and document the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]view in the ACE performance runbook.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-mj","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.5","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-mj.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-8bf0166e78b06053005821bc2d66afdb","started_at":"2026-08-16T00:28:30.185247+00:00","state":"completed"},{"commits":[{"committed_at":1786852130,"sha":"9a3a8617cac79b79217520fbc5ba8c33bde5f17b","subject":"feat(ace): render the Statistics Perf dashboard"}],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"chat":{"digest":"3e43957998b9f8f44a0d5d2602f69fc128fc3b5b2d5992d7e12880eefd9bfe03","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sas